<!--
  RUT_Miasma_ForgeOnSurvival.xml       UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M5 build pass

  Wires the already-spiked, already-compiling
  RM_HediffComp_ForgeOnSurvival/HediffCompProperties_ForgeOnSurvival
  (src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/RM_HediffComp_ForgeOnSurvival.cs)
  onto real disease HediffDefs for the first time — miasma_kit_spec.md M5:
  "surviving a disease in the Miasma sometimes leaves something behind."
  Confirmed that class needs no new field for this: onlyInBiomes,
  minPeakSeverity, noBoonWeight and boonOptions already cover everything the
  spec's own table calls for — no C# change to that class this pass.

  Targets: the 7 vanilla HediffDefs that actually carry
  HediffCompProperties_Immunizable (confirmed by reading Data/Core/Defs/
  HediffDefs/Hediffs_Local_Infections.xml directly this pass — GutWorms/
  MuscleParasites/FibrousMechanites/SensoryMechanites do NOT gain immunity
  and were excluded on purpose, since RM_HediffComp_ForgeOnSurvival's own
  removal gate is `ImmunityHandler.GetImmunity(parent.def) >= 1f`, which
  those hediffs can never reach): Flu, Animal_Flu, Plague, Animal_Plague,
  Malaria, SleepingSickness, WoundInfection. No Miasma-specific campaign
  disease HediffDef exists yet to patch alongside these — the one campaign
  disease family found in src/ this pass, RUT_RotSporeKit_Hediffs.xml
  (RUT_SporesBuildup/RUT_SporeFlesh/RUT_HediffSkulltopSpores), belongs to a
  different biome (the Rot) and is left alone; a Miasma-specific disease is
  roster/content-pass territory, not this item's to invent.

  onlyInBiomes gates by the pawn's CURRENT map biome at removal time (the
  comp's own runtime check), not by where the disease was caught — so this
  is deliberately biome-scoped to RUT_Miasma alone, exactly matching the
  sheet's "the Miasma, uniquely."

  Each disease gets its OWN boon table, not a shared one across all seven:
  the 30% slot names ONLY that disease's own RUT_HardenedImmunity_<disease>
  (surviving Plague can only ever forge plague-hardening, never
  flu-hardening) — the 14%/1% tiers are the same three/five generic hediffs
  for every disease, per the spec's own table. Weights: 55 (noBoonWeight) +
  30 (own HardenedImmunity) + 14 (split evenly across the 3 FeverForged
  minor hediffs, ~4.6667 each) + 1 (split evenly across the 5 strange-tier
  hediffs, 0.2 each) = 100, matching the spec's own percentages exactly.

  minPeakSeverity 0.6 is the class's own default, written out explicit here
  for citation (spec's own INVENTED value — "a brush with it doesn't
  forge").

  MayRequire on every added <li> (not just relying on the target disease's
  own def existing): the comp Class and boon HediffDefs referenced all live
  in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards / this same RUT content — if that mod
  is ever absent from a load order, an unresolvable comp Class risks
  discarding the WHOLE host disease def (the <li> trap, per this repo's own
  memory) rather than just this patch quietly not applying. PatchOperation
  Conditional guards each target disease existing at all (DLC/mod-order
  safety — "a patch that matches nothing logs nothing" is the hard-ban this
  repo tracks for exactly this shape of patch).
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/HediffDef[defName="Flu"]/comps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/HediffDef[defName="Flu"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.HediffCompProperties_ForgeOnSurvival" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
          <onlyInBiomes><li>RUT_Miasma</li></onlyInBiomes>
          <minPeakSeverity>0.6</minPeakSeverity>
          <noBoonWeight>55</noBoonWeight>
          <boonOptions>
            <li><hediff>RUT_HardenedImmunity_Flu</hediff><weight>30</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_FeverForged_Toughskin</hediff><weight>4.6667</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_FeverForged_Painworn</hediff><weight>4.6667</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_FeverForged_Saltblood</hediff><weight>4.6667</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_Miasma_SwarmMarked</hediff><weight>0.2</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_Miasma_SaltBlooded</hediff><weight>0.2</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_Miasma_LoamLunged</hediff><weight>0.2</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_Miasma_MotherDreamed</hediff><weight>0.2</weight></li>
            <li><hediff>RUT_Miasma_FeverTempered</hediff><weight>0.2</weight></li>
          </boonOptions>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

